input.prompt:
Check if the insights.db SQLite database has any data in the skill_signals table. Also check the sessions table to see if there are sessions at all.

Run these queries against .entire/insights.db:
1. SELECT COUNT(*) FROM skill_signals;
2. SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sessions;
3. SELECT * FROM skill_signals LIMIT 5;
4. SELECT DISTINCT agent FROM sessions;
5. Check the schema of skill_signals with .schema skill_signals

Also check .entire/skill-analytics.db:
1. SELECT COUNT(*) FROM skills;
2. SELECT COUNT(*) FROM skill_sessions;
3. SELECT * FROM skills LIMIT 5;
4. SELECT * FROM skill_sessions LIMIT 5;

This will tell us whether the issue is:
a) No sessions at all in insights.db
b) Sessions exist but skill_signals aren't being extracted
c) skill_signals exist but skill-analytics.db isn't reading them
d) Something else

Use bash with sqlite3 to query both databases.

